  "prediction": "This report provides an overview of cybersecurity-related legislation and hearings in the United States Congress during the 115th and 116th sessions. In the 116th Congress, the House and Senate have passed several cybersecurity bills, including four in the House and one in the Senate. These bills include measures to establish a cybersecurity institute, conduct a review of federal cybersecurity programs, and enhance cybersecurity information sharing. The report also highlights five significant cybersecurity laws passed in the 115th Congress, such as the National Defense Authorization Acts of 2017 and 2018, which established new cybersecurity initiatives and programs. The report concludes by listing cybersecurity-related hearings in the 116th Congress, arranged by date and committee, but notes that the list is not exhaustive. Overall, the report underscores the ongoing efforts of the U.S. Congress to address cybersecurity challenges through legislation and oversight.",
  "scored_prediction": "This report provides an overview of cybersecurity-related legislation and hearings in the United States Congress during the 115th and 116th sessions. In the 116th Congress, the House and Senate have passed several cybersecurity bills, including four in the House and one in the Senate. These bills include measures to establish a cybersecurity institute, conduct a review of federal cybersecurity programs, and enhance cybersecurity information sharing. The report also highlights five significant cybersecurity laws passed in the 115th Congress, such as the National Defense Authorization Acts of 2017 and 2018, which established new cybersecurity initiatives and programs. The report concludes by listing cybersecurity-related hearings in the 116th Congress, arranged by date and committee, but notes that the list is not exhaustive. Overall, the report underscores the ongoing efforts of the U.S. Congress to address cybersecurity challenges through legislation and oversight.",
  "score": 24.844720001234524,
  "answers": [
    "Most major cybersecurity legislative provisions were enacted prior to 2002, despite many recommendations having been made over the past decade. More recently, in the 115th and 116th Congresses, cybersecurity legislation has received either committee or floor action or final passage, and both chambers have held multiple hearings. In the 116th Congress, a number of House and Senate bills have received consideration, and hearings have been held by committees in each chamber. In the 115th Congress, 31 bills received some type of action (committee consideration or passage by one or both chambers). Five bills became public law. The House held 54 hearings on cybersecurity issues and the Senate held 40 hearings."
